// A binary operator with a floating-point operand. Both operands are converted
// to the type they meet at (long double if either is, else double if either is,
// else float), then crt's cfl_* does the operation on the words (cld_* on the
// addresses, for a long double: ld_bin_txt); a float result is rounded to binary32 after
// the operation, which is what C does with FLT_EVAL_METHOD 0 -- and for + - * /
// rounding the double result is exact, because a double holds more than twice a
// float's digits. A comparison answers 0 or 1, false for a NaN except for !=.
fl_is_bin(int id) {
  int ta = kid_ty((import na), id);
  int tb = kid_ty((import nb), id);
  int ok = fl_pair(ta, tb) >= 0;
} return int ok;
